我先说吗？

97
00:03:11.380 --> 00:03:11.620
Sure.
当然。

98
00:03:12.140 --> 00:03:14.180
Darby, I'm a little obsessed with Stonehenge.
达比，我对巨石阵有点着迷。

99
00:03:14.180 --> 00:03:14.660
Okay.
好吧。

100
00:03:15.200 --> 00:03:20.240
So, when I was in college, I did a semester abroad in London and I signed up for this bus tour.
所以，我上大学的时候，在伦敦参加了一个学期的海外交流项目，我报名了这个巴士旅行团。

101
00:03:20.480 --> 00:03:25.040
We loaded up on a bus and we drove to Stonehenge and I got goosebumps.
我们登上大巴车，开往巨石阵，我当时就起了一身鸡皮疙瘩。

102
00:03:25.580 --> 00:03:27.100
It was like foggy.
当时还起雾了。

103
00:03:27.400 --> 00:03:28.900
These things are huge.
这些东西太巨大了。

104
00:03:29.060 --> 00:03:29.580
They're huge.
它们真的太巨大了。

105
00:03:29.580 --> 00:03:33.220
I also took my ye olde camera and I took tons of pictures.
我还带上了我那老式的古董相机，拍了无数的照片。

106
00:03:33.880 --> 00:03:37.920
And then when I got back to my dorm room, I realized I hadn't put any film in it.
然后等我回到宿舍时，我才发现里面根本没装胶卷。

107
00:03:38.160 --> 00:03:38.600
Oh.
哦。

108
00:03:38.720 --> 00:03:39.680
I don't have a single picture.
我一张照片都没有。

109
00:03:40.340 --> 00:03:45.280
Well, what's the conspiracy about Stonehenge that it's arranged by like aliens or something?
话说，关于巨石阵有什么阴谋论吗？比如是什么外星人之类的人安排的？

110
00:03:45.440 --> 00:03:46.260
Like what is it?
到底是怎么回事？

111
00:03:46.260 --> 00:03:53.100
When you go and see it, it's hard to imagine how these stones got there, how they got upright.
当你亲自去看的时候，你很难想象这些石头是怎么到那里的，又是怎么立起来的。

112
00:03:53.460 --> 00:03:55.700
Does like nobody know how they got there?
难道就没有人知道它们是怎么到那儿的吗？

113
00:03:55.840 --> 00:03:58.560
Well, there's a lot of like different theories and things.
嗯，有很多不同的理论和说法。

114
00:03:58.700 --> 00:04:02.560
But the thing that I think really kicked off some conspiracy theories, at least from what
但我觉得真正引发一些阴谋论的东西，至少从我

115
00:04:02.560 --> 00:04:09.980
I saw online, is in 2024, the science journal called Nature revealed that the six-ton altar
在网上看到的来说，是在2024年，一本名为《自然》的科学杂志透露，巨石阵中那块六吨重的祭坛

116
00:04:09.980 --> 00:04:16.140
stone at Stonehenge came from the northeast of Scotland and not whales like the
石来自苏格兰东北部，而不是像该纪念碑的

117
00:04:16.140 --> 00:04:17.820
rest of the monument's blue stones.
其他青石那样来自威尔士。

118
00:04:18.020 --> 00:04:21.020
Wait, there's one stone that's different than all the other stones?
等等，有一块石头跟所有其他石头都不一样？

119
00:04:21.020 --> 00:04:21.380
Yes.
是的。

120
00:04:21.380 --> 00:04:27.160
And it's a pretty fascinating revelation because it really ignited the question, how
这是一个相当迷人的发现，因为它真正点燃了一个问题：

121
00:04:27.160 --> 00:04:32.380
were the stones, some weighing 45 tons, transported and arranged to where they sit today?
这些石头（有些重达45吨）当年是如何被运送到并排列到今天这个位置的？

122
00:04:32.780 --> 00:04:34.700
I mean, there was no basic transportation.
我的意思是，当时根本没有什么基础交通工具。

123
00:04:35.020 --> 00:04:36.980
The wheel hadn't even been invented.
轮子甚至都还没被发明出来。

124
00:04:37.140 --> 00:04:40.040
The wheel was like was invented five centuries later.
轮子好像是在五个世纪后才被发明的。

125
00:04:41.080 --> 00:04:42.200
Wait, what?
等一下，什么？

126
00:04:42.620 --> 00:04:43.160
Yeah, I know.
对，我知道。

127
00:04:43.160 --> 00:04:48.260
Well, so much of what scientists do know about the construction of Stonehenge is from educated
科学家对巨石阵建造过程的了解，很大程度上来自于有根据的

128
00:04:48.260 --> 00:04:54.720
guesses and constantly evolving research, the most recent of which suggests that, in fact,
猜测和不断演变的研究，其中最新的一项研究表明，事实上，

129
00:04:54.900 --> 00:04:59.880
two of the largest boulders that make up Stonehenge have always been there where they sit today,
构成巨石阵的两块最大的巨石一直都在它们今天所在的地方，

130
00:05:00.060 --> 00:05:02.120
but they don't know where the rest came from.
但他们不知道剩下的石头是从哪来的。

131
00:05:02.440 --> 00:05:06.760
And so theories are, if not aliens, perhaps giants.
所以各种理论认为，如果不是外星人，那也许就是巨人。

132
00:05:07.340 --> 00:05:07.940
Giants?
巨人？

133
00:05:08.020 --> 00:05:08.260
Yes!
对！

134
00:05:08.260 --> 00:05:09.540
One of the earliest-
最早期的——

135
00:05:09.540 --> 00:05:11.120
We used to be a land of giants?
我们以前是一片巨人的土地吗？

136
00:05:11.240 --> 00:05:16.420
Listen, one of the earliest names for Stonehenge was, and I'm going to say it wrong, guys,
听着，巨石阵最早的名字之一是——伙计们，我可能要读错了——

137
00:05:18.000 --> 00:05:19.040
Corea Gigantum.
Corea Gigantum。

138
00:05:19.400 --> 00:05:19.920
Okay.
好吧。

139
00:05:20.660 --> 00:05:23.980
Which has been interpreted by some as giants dance.
这被有些人解释为“巨人的舞蹈”。

140
00:05:25.440 --> 00:05:27.400
So, you know, I don't know.
所以，你知道的，我不知道。

141
00:05:28.060 --> 00:05:33.900
Is this, like, giving credibility to giants used to roam the Earth or aliens or who knows?
这是否赋予了“巨人曾漫步地球”或“外星人”之类的说法某种可信度，谁知道呢？

142
00:05:34.020 --> 00:05:40.980
But let me tell you, whoever arranged those was an amazing engineer to make all that happen.
但我要告诉你们，不管是谁排列了这些石头，都是个了不起的工程师，才能让这一切成为现实。

143
00:05:41.100 --> 00:05:42.000
