如果没有你，这就只能叫《屋顶》了。

805
00:32:04.230 --> 00:32:05.110
That's adorable.
太可爱了。

806
00:32:05.230 --> 00:32:06.170
That show needed you.
那场演出真需要你。

807
00:32:06.290 --> 00:32:07.090
That's adorable.
太可爱了。

808
00:32:07.150 --> 00:32:07.570
So cute.
太萌了。

809
00:32:08.170 --> 00:32:09.570
Well, Izzy, that was fantastic.
伊兹，刚才真是太棒了。

810
00:32:09.950 --> 00:32:11.450
Next up is Kelly M.
接下来是来自

811
00:32:11.630 --> 00:32:12.670
from London, UK.
英国伦敦的凯莉·M。

812
00:32:13.490 --> 00:32:14.370
Kelly says,
凯莉说，

813
00:32:14.370 --> 00:32:16.110
Dear ladies, Happy New Year.
亲爱的女士们，新年快乐。

814
00:32:16.290 --> 00:32:22.710
In news from London, I visited the Marie Antoinette style exhibition at the V&A Museum yesterday.
伦敦发来报道，我昨天去V&A博物馆参观了玛丽·安托瓦内特风格展。

815
00:32:23.010 --> 00:32:24.370
It was wonderful.
太精彩了。

816
00:32:24.750 --> 00:32:27.470
Items actually used by the queen.
展出的都是女王实际用过的物品。

817
00:32:28.010 --> 00:32:30.530
Chairs, desks, tea sets.
椅子、书桌、茶具。

818
00:32:30.870 --> 00:32:34.450
Finishing with a room filled with modern designs inspired by her.
最后是一个展厅，里面摆满了受她启发创作的现代设计。

819
00:32:35.010 --> 00:32:35.830
10 out of 10.
给满分10分。

820
00:32:36.210 --> 00:32:36.650
Recommend.
强烈推荐。

821
00:32:36.650 --> 00:32:39.370
Lots of love to you and the pod team from London.
来自伦敦的满满爱意送给你们和播客团队。

822
00:32:40.550 --> 00:32:43.550
This is making me want to get on an airplane right now and see this exhibit.
这让我现在就想坐上飞机去看看这个展览。

823
00:32:43.790 --> 00:32:45.230
I want to see the tea set.
我想看那套茶具。

824
00:32:45.570 --> 00:32:46.490
I want to see it all.
我什么都想看。

825
00:32:46.590 --> 00:32:47.210
I want to see it all.
我什么都想看。

826
00:32:47.310 --> 00:32:48.890
But I need to see the tea set.
但我最想看茶具。

827
00:32:49.870 --> 00:32:50.910
What are we going to do?
我们该怎么办？

828
00:32:51.090 --> 00:32:52.050
We're going to go to London.
我们要去伦敦。

829
00:32:52.310 --> 00:32:52.710
Are we?
是吗？

830
00:32:52.870 --> 00:32:54.390
Office ladies in London!
办公室女士去伦敦！

831
00:32:55.030 --> 00:33:00.390
Lady, we are having a hard time planning our one-day work retreat in town.
女士，我们连策划本市的一日工作静修都焦头烂额呢。

832
00:33:00.690 --> 00:33:01.110
I know.
我知道。

833
00:33:01.150 --> 00:33:02.270
How are we going to London?
我们怎么去得了伦敦？

834
00:33:02.270 --> 00:33:03.030
Well, we're busy.
好吧，我们很忙。

835
00:33:03.170 --> 00:33:05.090
We have five kids between the two of us.
我们俩加起来有五个孩子。

836
00:33:05.130 --> 00:33:05.410
I know.
我知道。

837
00:33:05.430 --> 00:33:05.930
We're busy.
我们很忙。

838
00:33:06.170 --> 00:33:08.710
But, I mean, Kelly, I'd love to get there.
但是，我是说，凯莉，我很想去那儿。

839
00:33:08.830 --> 00:33:09.570
Thanks for sharing.
谢谢你的分享。

840
00:33:09.790 --> 00:33:12.190
Thanks for writing in with your Around the Towns.
谢谢你发来“走过路过”栏目的来信。

841
00:33:12.270 --> 00:33:13.710
Let's get back to the episode.
让我们回到正片中来。

842
00:33:13.710 --> 00:33:17.190
Next up, Detrick lets us know that Nicole is really struggling.
接下来，德特里克告诉我们尼科尔真的很难受。

843
00:33:17.490 --> 00:33:21.430
I guess the kombucha that she drank was supposed to be refrigerated.
我猜她喝的那瓶康普茶本来是该冷藏的。

844
00:33:21.550 --> 00:33:22.790
She is not going to have a good time.
她这下有罪受了。

845
00:33:22.910 --> 00:33:25.410
She's going to spend a lot of this episode in the bathroom.
这一集她得有相当一部分时间泡在洗手间里了。

846
00:33:25.690 --> 00:33:26.090
Yes.
没错。

847
00:33:26.270 --> 00:33:27.390
Like, you know.
就，你懂的。

848
00:33:27.930 --> 00:33:33.290
And Esmeralda calls Frank Durham the administrative manager of McGundry Park.
然后埃斯梅拉达管麦甘德里公园的行政经理叫弗兰克·达勒姆。

849
00:33:34.230 --> 00:33:37.050
And he's very dismissive towards her.
而且他对她态度非常敷衍。

850
00:33:37.290 --> 00:33:38.090
He is.
确实如此。

851
00:33:38.270 --> 00:33:38.590
Yeah.
没错。

852
00:33:38.850 --> 00:33:40.830
He says, listen, that's what's happening.
他说，听着，事情就是这样。

853
00:33:40.830 --> 00:33:42.730
But Esmeralda is not dissuaded.
但埃斯梅拉达并没有被劝退。

854
00:33:42.730 --> 00:33:44.530
In fact, it emboldens her.
事实上，这反而给了她勇气。

855
00:33:44.690 --> 00:33:45.630
She's like, you know what?
她心想，你知道吗？

856
00:33:45.830 --> 00:33:47.130
There's a story here.
这儿有个故事。

857
00:33:47.290 --> 00:33:49.350
She thinks he was being dodgy on the phone.
她觉得他在电话里支支吾吾的。

858
00:33:49.550 --> 00:33:49.770
Yeah.
没错。

859
00:33:50.010 --> 00:33:54.070
So her and Mare are going to go down to the City Hall offices.
于是她和梅尔打算去市政厅办公室。

860
00:33:54.490 --> 00:33:55.430
And do some digging.
去挖点料。

861
00:33:55.790 --> 00:33:56.050
Yeah.
没错。

862
00:33:56.270 --> 00:34:02.490
They go tell Ned, who has this insane blue face mask on his face.
他们去告诉内德，他脸上敷着一个疯狂的蓝色面膜。

863
00:34:02.490 --> 00:34:05.690
Honestly, it looks like the blue version of the mask you bought us.
说实话，看起来就像你给我们买的那个面膜的蓝色版。

864
00:34:05.830 --> 00:34:10.030
Lady, this is what inspired me to get this mask, is Ned's blue mask.
女士，这就是我买这面膜的灵感来源，就是内德的蓝色面膜。

865
00:34:10.210 --> 00:34:11.210
And guess what?
你猜怎么着？

866
00:34:11.210 --> 00:34:12.450
You can get a blue one.
你可以买个蓝色的。

867
00:34:12.590 --> 00:34:13.710
It's like hydration.
就像补水一样。

868
00:34:13.950 --> 00:34:16.150
But I thought we should get the firming one.
但我觉得我们应该买紧致的。

869
00:34:16.390 --> 00:34:17.230
What are you saying?
你在说什么？

870
00:34:17.670 --> 00:34:18.470
What are you implying?
你在暗示什么？

871
00:34:18.630 --> 00:34:19.730
That's what we ever talk about.
我们平时聊的不就是这个吗。

872
00:34:19.870 --> 00:34:22.250
It's like, how do we firm up our wobbles?
就像，怎么才能让我们松弛的地方紧致起来？

873
00:34:22.670 --> 00:34:23.110
Anyway.
言归正传。

874
00:34:23.470 --> 00:34:25.150
Sam, sorry to lump you in that.
萨姆，抱歉把你扯进来了。

875
00:34:25.450 --> 00:34:26.030
No, I'm good.
没事，我挺好的。

876
00:34:28.050 --> 00:34:31.390
Well, all of Hollywood is firming up their wobbles.
好吧，整个好莱坞都在让松弛的地方变紧致。

877
00:34:31.390 --> 00:34:33.590
They're doing all the things and we've done nothing.
他们各种法子都试了，而我们什么都没做。

878
00:34:33.590 --> 00:34:35.110
What do they call it now?
他们现在管这叫什么来着？

879
00:34:35.290 --> 00:34:36.310
You look snatched.
你看上去很紧致。

880
00:34:36.450 --> 00:34:37.150
Oh, snatched.
哦，紧致。

881
00:34:37.330 --> 00:34:38.450
You look snatched.
你看上去很紧致。

882
00:34:38.590 --> 00:34:39.070
We're not snatched.
我们可一点都不紧致。

883
00:34:39.070 --> 00:34:41.290
You're all, your neck is all like tight.
你们全身上下，脖子紧绷绷的。

884
00:34:41.710 --> 00:34:43.990
What's the term if you're not snatched?
如果不够紧致，那个词叫什么？

885
00:34:44.150 --> 00:34:44.510
Us.
我们。

886
00:34:46.550 --> 00:34:47.470
Office ladies.
办公室女士。

887
00:34:49.010 --> 00:34:50.570
But here's my question.
但我的问题是。

888
00:34:50.570 --> 00:34:54.070
When you snatch up your face like that, when you do all that, right?
当你把脸部像那样提拉起来，当你做所有这些事情的时候，对吧？

889
00:34:54.250 --> 00:34:54.650
Yeah.
没错。

890
00:34:54.650 --> 00:34:56.010
What about your hands?
你的手怎么办？

891
00:34:56.310 --> 00:34:59.570
Do you still have old lady hands or are you snatching your hands?
你的手还是老太婆的手，还是说你连手也一起做紧致了？

892
00:34:59.710 --> 00:35:02.030
Here's what I told you when we were talking about this.
这就是我们聊起这个时我跟你说的话。

893
00:35:02.070 --> 00:35:04.650
I said, I feel like it's like my house.
我说，我觉得这就像我的房子。

894
00:35:04.750 --> 00:35:06.010
My house is an older house.
我的房子是一栋老房子。

895
00:35:06.230 --> 00:35:07.170
Well, guess what?
好吧，你猜怎么着？

896
00:35:07.290 --> 00:35:08.950
We've got a leak in Kate's bathroom.
凯特的浴室漏水了。

897
00:35:09.150 --> 00:35:10.890
It's going to have to be gutted and redone.
不得不拆掉重装了。

898
00:35:11.170 --> 00:35:13.430
And now Kate's bathroom is going to look amazing.
现在凯特的浴室看起来会棒极了。

899
00:35:13.770 --> 00:35:16.190
And the rest of the house is going to look like shit.
而房子的其他地方看起来就像一堆狗屎。

900
00:35:16.530 --> 00:35:17.410
So this is what happens.
事情就是这样。

901
00:35:17.530 --> 00:35:21.730
You like fix up one part and then the rest that isn't working is very obvious.
你修好了一个地方，然后其他没修好的地方就变得特别显眼。

902
00:35:22.270 --> 00:35:22.710
Yeah.
对。

903
00:35:22.910 --> 00:35:24.110
It's a slippery slope.
这是一个无底洞。

904
00:35:24.110 --> 00:35:27.610
So like if I did my neck, then what about my eyebrow, my forehead?
所以，如果我做了脖子，那我的眉毛、额头怎么办？

905
00:35:27.910 --> 00:35:28.550
I don't know.
我不知道。

906
00:35:29.070 --> 00:35:30.330
It's a domino effect.
这就像多米诺骨牌效应。

907
00:35:30.690 --> 00:35:30.950
Yeah.
对。

908
00:35:31.190 --> 00:35:34.590
Well, that's why I guess you have to do like it all at once.
嗯，我想这就是为什么你得一次性全做了。

909
00:35:34.930 --> 00:35:35.210
Yeah.
对。

910
00:35:35.370 --> 00:35:36.690
Seems traumatic to me.
我觉得这太受罪了。

911
00:35:36.970 --> 00:35:37.210
Yeah.
对。

912
00:35:37.350 --> 00:35:38.110
And painful.
而且很痛苦。

913
00:35:38.450 --> 00:35:38.730
Yeah.
对。

914
00:35:38.910 --> 00:35:39.690
And expensive.
而且很贵。

915
00:35:40.090 --> 00:35:41.310
And so expensive.
而且贵得离谱。

916
00:35:42.010 --> 00:35:42.330
Yeah.
对。

917
00:35:42.730 --> 00:35:45.110
I mean, for that amount of money, just retire.
我的意思是，花那么多钱，不如直接退休算了。

918
00:35:45.290 --> 00:35:46.070
Go off the grid.
隐居避世。

919
00:35:46.450 --> 00:35:47.930
I won't be in TV.
我才不在电视上露面呢。

920
00:35:48.370 --> 00:35:49.290
Like, who cares?
谁在乎呢？

921
00:35:49.510 --> 00:35:50.070
I know.
我懂。

922
00:35:50.850 --> 00:35:51.630
No kidding.
可不是嘛。

923
00:35:51.970 --> 00:35:52.650
My gosh.
我的天呐。

924
00:35:52.890 --> 00:35:53.230
All right.
好吧。

925
00:35:53.230 --> 00:35:59.850
Anyway, one of the things that does happen, though, is part of Ned's face mask, a clump of
言归正传，不过其中发生的一件事是，内德的面膜掉了一块

926
00:35:59.850 --> 00:36:02.510
it falls on his shirt and he rubs it off.
在衬衫上，他把它擦掉了。

927
00:36:02.630 --> 00:36:05.090
And where it landed, it bleaches his shirt.
而在它掉落的地方，把衬衫给漂白了。

928
00:36:05.290 --> 00:36:07.070
So now he's freaking out.
所以他现在吓坏了。

929
00:36:07.190 --> 00:36:12.550
This is foreshadowing for how this face mask is going to go, by the way.
顺便说一句，这预示着这款面膜接下来会发生什么。

930
00:36:13.090 --> 00:36:15.030
So now we're going to go to City Hall.
所以现在我们要去市政厅。

931
00:36:15.270 --> 00:36:18.670
Maren Esmeralda are talking to the City Hall receptioniSt.
玛伦·埃斯梅拉达正在和市政厅前台接待员交谈。

932
00:36:19.170 --> 00:36:25.450
They're like, OK, so there was a hearing about the bathroom closure on the 13th.
他们说，好的，13号有一场关于关闭洗手间的听证会。

933
00:36:25.570 --> 00:36:26.830
This was all on the up and up.
这一切都是光明正大的。

934
00:36:26.990 --> 00:36:28.190
This closing of the bathroom.
关闭洗手间这件事。

935
00:36:28.430 --> 00:36:30.170
This was approved by a vote.
这是投票表决通过的。

936
00:36:30.570 --> 00:36:30.770
Yeah.
对。

937
00:36:32.250 --> 00:36:33.610
Esmeralda's still not convinced.
埃斯梅拉达还是不太相信。

938
00:36:33.610 --> 00:36:38.150
She sort of fakes this giant migraine and then she goes off into his office.
她假装得了严重的偏头痛，然后溜进了他的办公室。

939
00:36:38.290 --> 00:36:40.130
She gets his day planner.
她拿了他的日程规划本。

940
00:36:40.390 --> 00:36:42.010
She takes a picture of it.
她拍了张照片。

941
00:36:42.170 --> 00:36:42.490
Yes.
是的。

942
00:36:42.610 --> 00:36:47.550
And she sees that he was doing a trivia night whenever this meeting took place.
她发现开会的时候他去参加知识问答之夜了。

943
00:36:47.550 --> 00:36:49.390
He wasn't even there, this Frank Durham guy.
这个叫弗兰克·达勒姆的家伙根本不在那儿。

944
00:36:49.630 --> 00:36:50.150
Exactly.
没错。

945
00:36:51.150 --> 00:36:56.110
I want to give a shout out to Leslie Thurston, who played the City Hall administrator.
我要特别感谢莱斯莉·瑟斯顿，她饰演市政厅管理员。

946
00:36:56.530 --> 00:36:57.510
She was great.
她演得太棒了。

947
00:36:57.770 --> 00:36:58.930
She studied at Groundlings.
她曾在爆笑剧团学习过。

948
00:36:58.930 --> 00:37:03.590
She's been in a gazillion TV shows, including Parks and Rec and The Morning Show.
她演过无数电视剧，包括《公园与游憩》和《早间新闻》。

949
00:37:03.770 --> 00:37:06.530
And I've also got a little location breakdown for you.
我还要为大家简单介绍一下拍摄地点。

950
00:37:07.150 --> 00:37:12.650
Eric said Frank Durham's office in City Hall was shot at the Freemasons Hall in Pasadena.
埃里克说市政厅里弗兰克·达勒姆的办公室是在帕萨迪纳的共济会大厅拍摄的。

951
00:37:13.510 --> 00:37:17.990
He went on to say, I don't want to make any enemies of the Freemasons, but I think that
接着他又说：“我不想跟共济会结仇，但我认为那栋

952
00:37:17.990 --> 00:37:18.870
building is haunted.
建筑闹鬼。”

953
00:37:19.710 --> 00:37:20.890
I looked it up.
我查了一下。

954
00:37:21.050 --> 00:37:23.110
We were talking about conspiracies earlier.
我们刚才还在聊阴谋论呢。

955
00:37:24.490 --> 00:37:28.670
I could find nothing about the Freemasons Hall in Pasadena being haunted.
我没查到任何关于帕萨迪纳共济会会所闹鬼的说法。

956
00:37:28.930 --> 00:37:34.270
But did you know Pasadena, California is like the most haunted section of Los Angeles?
但你知道吗，加州帕萨迪纳简直是洛杉矶最闹鬼的地区？

957
00:37:34.750 --> 00:37:40.730
They've got a gazillion buildings and parks that all have stories of being haunted and
他们有无数的建筑和公园，都有闹鬼和

958
00:37:40.730 --> 00:37:41.110
ghosts.
鬼魂的故事。

959
00:37:41.310 --> 00:37:45.490
There's this one park that people say is haunted by the Marx Brothers.
有个公园，据说有马克思兄弟的鬼魂出没。

960
00:37:46.230 --> 00:37:46.750
Wow.
哇。

961
00:37:47.130 --> 00:37:47.350
Yeah.
对啊。

962
00:37:47.690 --> 00:37:51.170
I bet you could do like a haunted walking tour of Pasadena.
我敢说你可以办个帕萨迪纳闹鬼步行游览团。

963
00:37:51.270 --> 00:37:51.930
You probably could.
你大概还真行。

964
00:37:52.030 --> 00:37:53.650
Our driving tour is kind of spread out.
我们的车载观光路线有点分散。

965
00:37:53.730 --> 00:37:54.170
You could.
完全可以。

966
00:37:54.350 --> 00:37:54.490
Yeah.
是啊。

967
00:37:55.710 --> 00:37:56.650
Oh, lady.
哦，天哪。

968
00:37:56.870 --> 00:37:59.910
Can I also say my favorite Esmeralda line?
我能顺便说一下我最喜欢的埃斯梅拉达台词吗？

969
00:38:00.070 --> 00:38:04.070
When she's showing Mare the pictures of her calendar, now they're like outside.
当她向梅尔展示她日历的照片时，现在他们好像在室外了。

970
00:38:04.250 --> 00:38:05.170
They're in the parking lot.
他们在停车场。

971
00:38:05.450 --> 00:38:07.090
And they're like, look at this.
然后他们说，你看这个。

972
00:38:07.170 --> 00:38:08.430
There's no mention of a hearing.
上面根本没提听证会的事。

973
00:38:08.630 --> 00:38:09.770
Only trivia night.
只有琐事问答之夜。

974
00:38:09.930 --> 00:38:14.770
And then Esmeralda says, yes, those kinds of men, they love to yell out facts.
接着埃斯梅拉达说：“没错，那种男人，就喜欢大声喊出各种事实。”

975
00:38:15.750 --> 00:38:17.570
It's like a very funny thing.
这简直太搞笑了。

976
00:38:17.970 --> 00:38:23.070
Well, did you notice the star sticker on her phone and all the stickers on her car, which
对了，你注意到她手机上的星星贴纸，以及她车上的所有贴纸了吗？

977
00:38:23.070 --> 00:38:25.110
looks like it's a Fiat 500X.
那辆车看起来像是一辆菲亚特 500X。

978
00:38:25.130 --> 00:38:25.910
I looked it up.
我查过了。

979
00:38:26.130 --> 00:38:27.530
Her car is also red.
她的车也是红色的。

980
00:38:27.710 --> 00:38:29.690
I feel like this red color is a theme for her.
我觉得这红色是她的一个主题色。

981
00:38:29.870 --> 00:38:31.910
She almost always has a hint of red.
她几乎总是带着一抹红色。

982
00:38:32.430 --> 00:38:39.210
Red yo-yo, red flowers on her blouse, red lipstick, red dress, red car, and stars are everywhere.
红色的溜溜球、衬衫上的红花、红唇、红裙子、红汽车，而且到处都是星星。

983
00:38:40.070 --> 00:38:43.710
Lady, I became obsessed with these stars like two episodes ago.
天哪，我大概在两集前就开始对这些星星着迷了。

984
00:38:43.890 --> 00:38:44.210
I know.
我知道。

985
00:38:44.310 --> 00:38:47.870
When I did a breakdown of her office, I mentioned they're on all kinds of things.
当我盘点她的办公室时，我提到它们出现在各种东西上。

986
00:38:48.010 --> 00:38:50.170
There's a star sticker on the lamp, on her frame.
台灯上有星星贴纸，相框上也有。

987
00:38:50.350 --> 00:38:51.770
And they seem to be expanding.
而且它们似乎还在增多。

988
00:38:52.050 --> 00:38:53.610
I feel like I keep noticing more.
我觉得我不断发现更多。

989
00:38:53.750 --> 00:38:57.610
And like you said, I noticed them on her phone and her car.
正如你所说，我在她的手机和车上也注意到了。

990
00:38:57.810 --> 00:38:58.770
I reached out to Chelsea.
我联系了切尔西。

991
00:38:59.250 --> 00:39:00.110
Chelsea Frye.
切尔西·弗莱。

992
00:39:00.270 --> 00:39:01.470
Oh, what did Chelsea say?
哦，切尔西怎么说？

993
00:39:01.470 --> 00:39:02.350
What's the scoop?
有什么内幕？

994
00:39:02.590 --> 00:39:04.230
Chelsea, talk to me about these stars.
切尔西，快跟我聊聊这些星星的事。

995
00:39:04.610 --> 00:39:07.730
Because I feel like this was Sabrina.
因为我觉得这可能是萨布丽娜的主意。

996
00:39:09.210 --> 00:39:11.590
Can you find out, was it her?
你能查查是她吗？

997
00:39:11.770 --> 00:39:12.850
Was it set decoration?
是布景装饰吗？

998
00:39:13.190 --> 00:39:14.450
It's so specific.
这太具体了。

999
00:39:14.890 --> 00:39:16.250
Chelsea was like, I'm on it.
切尔西当时说：“包在我身上。”

1000
00:39:17.910 --> 00:39:19.910
So here's what she found out.
所以这是她查到的结果。

1001
00:39:20.570 --> 00:39:25.290
Sabrina said it started with an email between herself and set decoration,
萨布丽娜说，事情是从她和布景部门之间的一封邮件开始的，

1002
00:39:25.290 --> 00:39:28.570
just talking about what Esmeralda's office might look like.
当时只是在讨论埃斯梅拉达的办公室可能会是什么样。

1003
00:39:28.830 --> 00:39:32.290
And Sabrina had really wanted the office to look personalized.
而且萨布丽娜非常希望办公室能展现出个性化。

1004
00:39:32.290 --> 00:39:38.190
So she brought in this sticker tape of stars.
所以她带去了这种星星形状的标签贴纸。

1005
00:39:38.630 --> 00:39:39.070
Okay.
好吧。

1006
00:39:39.330 --> 00:39:41.750
Because Sabrina herself has always loved stars.
因为萨布丽娜本人一直都很喜欢星星。

1007
00:39:41.750 --> 00:39:44.090
And she thought this was a really good overlap with her character.
她觉得这与她的角色有着非常好的契合度。

1008
00:39:44.430 --> 00:39:49.550
So they just let her start putting these stars wherever she wanted.
所以他们就让她开始把这些星星贴在她想贴的任何地方。

1009
00:39:49.550 --> 00:39:52.910
And she stuck them on everything, including the car.
而且她把它们贴在了所有东西上，包括车上。

1010
00:39:53.110 --> 00:39:55.590
Sabrina stuck them on the car.
萨布丽娜把它们贴在了车上。

1011
00:39:55.750 --> 00:39:57.010
There's so many.
真的有好多。

1012
00:39:57.010 --> 00:40:00.110
They like outline her window, her driver's door.
它们像是勾勒出了她的车窗和驾驶员车门的外轮廓。

1013
00:40:00.330 --> 00:40:02.230
So did she stick one or two on the car?
那她是在车上贴了一两张吗？

1014
00:40:02.390 --> 00:40:04.650
And then set deck was like, okay, we'll take it from here.
然后布景组就说，好吧，剩下的交给我们了。

1015
00:40:04.770 --> 00:40:06.070
No, I think she did it.
不，我觉得是她自己贴的。

1016
00:40:06.170 --> 00:40:07.590
I mean, I'm not 100% sure.
我是说，我不是百分之百确定。

1017
00:40:07.710 --> 00:40:08.930
But Chelsea was like, no, no, no.
但切尔西却说，不，不，不。

1018
00:40:09.210 --> 00:40:11.490
Sabrina stuck the stars on the car.
是萨布丽娜把星星贴在车上的。

1019
00:40:11.590 --> 00:40:12.410
Holy crap.
我的天呐。

1020
00:40:12.690 --> 00:40:13.090
I know.
我知道。

1021
00:40:13.450 --> 00:40:13.930
Isn't that crazy?
是不是很疯狂？

1022
00:40:14.110 --> 00:40:16.930
I also have to point out something else from this scene.
我还要指出这个场景中的另一个细节。

1023
00:40:18.230 --> 00:40:21.430
Did you notice that Mare's phone screen was cracked?
你注意到梅尔的手机屏幕碎了吗？

1024
00:40:21.710 --> 00:40:25.250
They FaceTimed Ned to tell him about this find.
他们给内德视频通话，把这个发现告诉了他。

1025
00:40:25.250 --> 00:40:28.610
And I just loved that little detail that Mare's screen has cracked.
我太喜欢梅尔手机屏幕碎了这一个小细节了。

1026
00:40:28.910 --> 00:40:29.790
She hasn't fixed it.
她一直没去修。

1027
00:40:29.850 --> 00:40:30.910
It's so relatable.
这太接地气了。

1028
00:40:31.170 --> 00:40:31.450
I know.
我懂。

1029
00:40:31.910 --> 00:40:36.370
Well, I also wanted to point out, since they're filming outside, it's in a parking lot.
嗯，我还想指出的是，既然他们是在室外拍摄，那是在一个停车场里。

1030
00:40:36.570 --> 00:40:40.050
We filmed outside in parking lots in the summer in Los Angeles.
我们在洛杉矶夏天室外的停车场里拍过戏。

1031
00:40:40.050 --> 00:40:42.170
They're dressed in jackets and winter wear.
他们穿着夹克和冬装。

1032
00:40:42.390 --> 00:40:45.870
And Eric shared with us that the week they filmed this episode,
埃里克跟我们分享说，他们拍这一集的那个星期，

1033
00:40:45.870 --> 00:40:49.430
it was crazy hot with temperatures over 100 degrees.
热得发疯，气温超过了100华氏度。

1034
00:40:49.770 --> 00:40:50.510
Oh, my gosh.
哦，天哪。

1035
00:40:50.670 --> 00:40:50.870
Yeah.
是啊。

1036
00:40:50.870 --> 00:40:55.350
And he said that he and Jason Wolliner, the director of this episode,
他说他和本集的导演杰森·沃利纳，

1037
00:40:55.610 --> 00:40:58.050
they decided to do a food truck that week.
他们决定那个星期搞一辆餐车。

1038
00:40:58.190 --> 00:40:58.450
Right?
对吧？

1039
00:40:58.730 --> 00:40:58.970
Yeah.
对的。

1040
00:40:59.110 --> 00:40:59.570
So nice.
太贴心了。

1041
00:40:59.730 --> 00:41:00.290
So nice.
太棒了。

1042
00:41:00.290 --> 00:41:01.650
For the crew, for everyone.
为了剧组，为了每个人。

1043
00:41:02.010 --> 00:41:04.310
And they picked a poutine truck.
而且他们选了一辆肉汁奶酪薯条餐车。

1044
00:41:04.870 --> 00:41:05.850
What's poutine?
什么是肉汁奶酪薯条？

1045
00:41:06.630 --> 00:41:07.550
How would you have it?
里面都有什么？

1046
00:41:07.630 --> 00:41:10.370
I mean, it's like French fries with like stuff on it,
就是炸薯条上面放了些东西，

1047
00:41:10.450 --> 00:41:12.730
like gravy and cheese curds.
比如肉汁和干酪块。

1048
00:41:12.790 --> 00:41:12.910
Oh, yeah.
哦，对。

1049
00:41:12.910 --> 00:41:13.830
But the gravy's like hot.
不过肉汁是热的。

1050
00:41:14.030 --> 00:41:14.290
Okay.
好吧。

1051
00:41:14.290 --> 00:41:16.690
Yeah, they have those in Amsterdam, too.
对，阿姆斯特丹也有那种。

1052
00:41:16.950 --> 00:41:17.250
Yeah.
对。

1053
00:41:17.730 --> 00:41:17.970
Okay.
好。

1054
00:41:18.450 --> 00:41:22.670
He said this poutine truck arrived on the hottest day of the year.
他说这辆肉汁奶酪薯条餐车偏偏在一年中最热的那天开来。

1055
00:41:24.070 --> 00:41:32.070
He said so people were having to eat hot duck gravy over French fries in like triple digit weather.
他说当时天气有华氏上百度，人们不得不在这种天气里吃浇着烫鸭肉汁的炸薯条。

1056
00:41:32.350 --> 00:41:32.670
Yum.
真美味。

1057
00:41:32.910 --> 00:41:34.470
He said not great.
他说感觉不太妙。

1058
00:41:37.590 --> 00:41:39.850
Well, it's getting close to the end of the day.
好吧，这一天快要结束了。

1059
00:41:40.070 --> 00:41:42.950
And Ned has gathered most of the staff into his office.
内德把大部分员工都叫到了他的办公室里。

1060
00:41:43.470 --> 00:41:49.170
And it is revealed that he has burned his face from this face mask thing.
结果发现他的脸被那个面膜之类的东西给烧伤了。

1061
00:41:50.230 --> 00:41:53.130
He also started taking everyone else's products.
他还开始拿走其他所有人的产品。

1062
00:41:53.350 --> 00:41:54.250
Like he went overboard.
简直是走火入魔了。

1063
00:41:54.530 --> 00:41:56.890
Yeah, because they were like, we can't do this anymore.
对，因为他们当时觉得，我们再也受不了了。

1064
00:41:57.010 --> 00:41:57.910
They were bailing.
他们都要跑路了。

1065
00:41:58.070 --> 00:41:58.330
Yes.
是的。

1066
00:41:58.450 --> 00:42:00.570
And he was like, I'm going to do everything.
而他的反应是，我要包揽一切。

1067
00:42:00.570 --> 00:42:10.030
Lady, watching him put that lighted chin strap over his burned face and then drinking the kombucha.
天哪，看他把那个带灯光的下巴束带戴在他烧伤的脸上，然后又喝着康普茶。

1068
00:42:10.030 --> 00:42:11.710
It was like wound on wound for you.
对你来说简直是伤口上撒盐。

1069
00:42:11.750 --> 00:42:14.110
It was the same as someone getting punched in a wound.
就跟有人往伤口上打一拳一样。

1070
00:42:14.290 --> 00:42:14.590
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1071
00:42:14.790 --> 00:42:15.290
It really...
真的……

1072
00:42:15.290 --> 00:42:16.190
I thought about you.
我当时就想到了你。

1073
00:42:16.350 --> 00:42:16.890
Thank you.
谢谢你。

1074
00:42:17.610 --> 00:42:19.170
Well, now we're at the bar.
好了，现在我们来到酒吧了。

1075
00:42:19.490 --> 00:42:21.330
I mean, Mare's going to go undercover.
我是说，梅尔要去做卧底了。

1076
00:42:21.790 --> 00:42:23.910
Esmeralda has given her a makeover in the bathroom.
埃斯梅拉达在洗手间里给她做了个大变身。

1077
00:42:24.090 --> 00:42:25.130
She looks amazing.
她看起来棒极了。

1078
00:42:25.490 --> 00:42:28.510
Do you think that is one of Esmeralda's dresses?
你觉得那会是埃斯梅拉达的裙子吗？

1079
00:42:28.970 --> 00:42:29.250
Yes.
是的。

1080
00:42:29.370 --> 00:42:30.290
This was my question.
这就是我的疑问。

1081
00:42:30.570 --> 00:42:30.850
I totally do.
我完全这么觉得。

1082
00:42:30.850 --> 00:42:33.230
It looks like Mare is wearing an Esmeralda dress.
看起来梅尔穿的就是埃斯梅拉达的裙子。

1083
00:42:33.290 --> 00:42:36.690
It's got kind of the Esmeralda belt look to it.
那条裙子隐约带有一种埃斯梅拉达风格的腰带。

1084
00:42:36.830 --> 00:42:36.990
Yeah.
对。

1085
00:42:37.450 --> 00:42:38.250
Ned shows up.
内德出现了。

1086
00:42:38.350 --> 00:42:39.650
He's like, why is she dressed like that?
他说，她怎么穿成这样？

1087
00:42:39.810 --> 00:42:42.910
And Esmeralda says she's undercover as a beautiful woman.
埃斯梅拉达说她是在假扮一个美女进行卧底。

1088
00:42:43.110 --> 00:42:43.770
I know.
我知道。

1089
00:42:44.430 --> 00:42:46.150
And Mare is working it, man.
而且梅尔可真放得开啊。

1090
00:42:46.270 --> 00:42:51.350
She got Frank to confirm that he does do trivia every Tuesday night, including the 13th.
她让弗兰克确认了他确实每周二晚上都参加益智问答之夜，包括13号那天。

1091
00:42:51.650 --> 00:42:53.070
This is very exciting.
这太令人兴奋了。

1092
00:42:53.370 --> 00:42:54.250
Very exciting.
非常兴奋。

1093
00:42:54.590 --> 00:42:55.970
They're exposing him.
他们在揭穿他。

1094
00:42:56.250 --> 00:43:00.210
I was curious about popular trivia game nights at bars.
我对酒吧里流行的益智问答游戏之夜很好奇。

1095
00:43:00.210 --> 00:43:01.090
What about them?
怎么说？

1096
00:43:01.430 --> 00:43:03.010
Well, I've never been to one.
嗯，我从来没去过。

1097
00:43:03.370 --> 00:43:04.550
And you know what?
而且你知道吗？

1098
00:43:04.630 --> 00:43:11.470
I found a website called Best Trivia Ever, and it lists different trivia themes and trivia night schedules nationwide.
我发现了一个叫做“史上最佳问答”的网站，上面列出了全国各地不同的问答主题和问答之夜的时间表。

1099
00:43:12.330 --> 00:43:13.430
They're very popular.
它们非常受欢迎。

1100
00:43:13.710 --> 00:43:14.390
They're so popular.
太受欢迎了。

1101
00:43:14.510 --> 00:43:16.910
But, lady, I didn't realize how many different types of genres.
但是，女士，我以前没意识到有这么多不同的流派。

1102
00:43:17.170 --> 00:43:21.070
I mean, obviously, there's sports, movies, books, musicians, animation, television.
我的意思是，显然有体育、电影、书籍、音乐人、动画、电视。

1103
00:43:21.530 --> 00:43:23.270
I mean, we know there's an office one.
我是说，我们知道有个关于《办公室》的知识问答。

1104
00:43:23.590 --> 00:43:23.690
Yeah.
对。

1105
00:43:23.690 --> 00:43:25.010
There's also, like, eras.
还有那种按年代划分的。

1106
00:43:25.210 --> 00:43:28.230
Like, there's 90s night, 80s nights trivia.
比如，有90年代之夜、80年代之夜的知识问答。

1107
00:43:30.110 --> 00:43:32.230
But listen to some of these categories.
但你听听其中一些类别。

1108
00:43:32.470 --> 00:43:33.430
I just want to read you a few.
我只想读几个给你听。

1109
00:43:34.610 --> 00:43:36.130
They sound like so much fun to me.
我觉得它们听起来太有意思了。

1110
00:43:36.890 --> 00:43:38.530
Action movie trivia night.
动作电影知识问答之夜。

1111
00:43:39.930 --> 00:43:41.770
Celebrity couples trivia night.
名人情侣知识问答之夜。

1112
00:43:42.650 --> 00:43:44.510
Stoner movie trivia night.
瘾君子电影知识问答之夜。

1113
00:43:44.810 --> 00:43:45.050
Okay.
好吧。

1114
00:43:45.510 --> 00:43:47.730
It's all movies where they think people get stoned.
这全都是关于人们抽大麻的电影。

1115
00:43:48.410 --> 00:43:50.750
Or are they movies you watch when you're stoned?
还是说这是你抽大麻时看的电影？

1116
00:43:50.750 --> 00:43:52.850
I think they're movies where people are stoned.
我觉得是关于人们抽大麻的电影。

1117
00:43:53.150 --> 00:43:54.610
I feel like it's both.
我觉得两者皆有。

1118
00:43:54.830 --> 00:43:55.230
Could be.
有可能。

1119
00:43:55.850 --> 00:43:58.490
Next one, Nicolas Cage trivia night.
下一个，尼古拉斯·凯奇知识问答之夜。

1120
00:43:58.810 --> 00:44:00.210
Is there a Keanu one?
有基努·里维斯的吗？

1121
00:44:00.390 --> 00:44:01.510
I'm sure there is.
我敢肯定有。

1122
00:44:01.650 --> 00:44:03.990
And, Sam, there's an Emily in Paris trivia night.
而且，萨姆，还有一个《艾米丽在巴黎》知识问答之夜。

1123
00:44:04.230 --> 00:44:04.670
Good.
不错。

1124
00:44:04.950 --> 00:44:06.630
You would destroy that night.
你在那个主题之夜绝对能大杀四方。

1125
00:44:07.410 --> 00:44:10.930
Anyway, I just was very tickled that there's so many types.
总之，有这么多类型，我感到非常开心。

1126
00:44:11.730 --> 00:44:14.010
We've been talking forever about doing one.
我们一直说要办一场，却总也办不成。

1127
00:44:14.130 --> 00:44:15.050
We never do it.
我们从来没行动过。

1128
00:44:15.470 --> 00:44:17.130
I mean, which one would you do?
我是说，你会参加哪一个？

1129
00:44:17.290 --> 00:44:18.890
I don't think we can do the office one.
我觉得我们没法参加《办公室》那个。

1130
00:44:18.890 --> 00:44:24.770
I wouldn't do well in the office one unless we got my friend, who I did Ashland Avenue
我在《办公室》那个问答上表现不会好，除非我们带上我的朋友威尔，我和他一起做过阿什兰大街节目

1131
00:44:24.770 --> 00:44:30.330
with, Will, who won the National Office Trivia ConteSt.
他赢得了全国《办公室》知识问答比赛。

1132
00:44:30.550 --> 00:44:33.690
Well, I think we would have to take Will and Billie Eilish.
好吧，我觉得我们得带上威尔和比莉·艾利什。

1133
00:44:34.270 --> 00:44:38.150
And then also, from Boy Meets World, we'd need to take Will Friedel.
然后还有《男孩世界》里的威尔·弗里德尔，我们也得带上。

1134
00:44:38.730 --> 00:44:40.350
He has a photographic memory.
他有过目不忘的记忆力。

1135
00:44:40.550 --> 00:44:41.550
Well, then we would win.
那我们就能赢了。

1136
00:44:41.670 --> 00:44:42.390
Then we would win.
那我们就能赢了。

1137
00:44:42.570 --> 00:44:44.910
But non-office trivia night?
但如果不是《办公室》主题的知识问答之夜呢？

1138
00:44:45.130 --> 00:44:47.230
I would do good at a horror movie trivia night.
我在恐怖电影知识问答之夜会表现得不错。

1139
00:44:47.230 --> 00:44:48.270
They have that genre.
他们有这个流派。

1140
00:44:48.510 --> 00:44:49.710
I think I could do really well.
我觉得我能表现得非常好。

1141
00:44:49.870 --> 00:44:50.030
Yeah.
对。

1142
00:44:50.390 --> 00:44:54.110
Although I'm not up on a lot of the more recent horror filMs.
虽然我对很多比较近期的恐怖电影不太了解。

1143
00:44:54.130 --> 00:44:56.870
I could do, like, horror films in history.
我可以说，比如历史上的恐怖电影。

1144
00:44:57.150 --> 00:44:57.370
Yeah.
对。

1145
00:44:57.830 --> 00:45:01.750
I mean, we might do well at, like, 80s or 90s pop culture.
我的意思是，我们在80年代或90年代流行文化方面可能会表现不错。

1146
00:45:03.190 --> 00:45:03.630
Right?
对吧？

1147
00:45:03.930 --> 00:45:05.210
Sam, have you seen Primate?
萨姆，你看过《灵长类》吗？

1148
00:45:05.770 --> 00:45:06.550
No, I haven't.
没有，我没看过。

1149
00:45:06.550 --> 00:45:06.950
Is it good?
好看吗？

1150
00:45:07.090 --> 00:45:07.610
I don't know.
我不知道。

1151
00:45:07.890 --> 00:45:08.230
What's it?
这是什么？

1152
00:45:08.230 --> 00:45:09.110
It's a horror movie, right?
是一部恐怖电影吧？

1153
00:45:09.190 --> 00:45:10.730
Is it about primates that take over?
讲的是灵长类动物占领地球吗？

1154
00:45:10.870 --> 00:45:14.570
It's about a single pet chimp that turns.
讲的是一只宠物黑猩猩突然发狂的故事。

1155
00:45:15.070 --> 00:45:17.070
And, I mean, this is a total fear of mine.
而且，我是说，这完全是我的心魔。

1156
00:45:17.590 --> 00:45:17.970
Like, the minute...
比如，就在那一刻……

1157
00:45:17.970 --> 00:45:19.410
I mean, you shouldn't be that afraid.
我是说，你没必要那么害怕。

1158
00:45:19.410 --> 00:45:21.110
I don't think you're ever going to have a pet chimp.
我觉得你这辈子都不会养宠物黑猩猩。

1159
00:45:21.190 --> 00:45:23.050
Well, you guys know I've had so many monkeys...
好吧，你们都知道我养过好多猴子……

1160
00:45:23.050 --> 00:45:25.110
There's so many ways to avoid this scenario.
有很多方法可以避免这种事发生。

1161
00:45:25.450 --> 00:45:26.850
I've had so many monkeys attack me.
我有过好多次被猴子袭击的经历。

1162
00:45:27.070 --> 00:45:27.750
You know this.
你知道这事的。

1163
00:45:28.030 --> 00:45:28.730
No, I don't.
不，我不知道。

1164
00:45:29.450 --> 00:45:29.990
Come on.
拜托。

1165
00:45:30.010 --> 00:45:31.470
I did an open mic night.
我参加过一次开放麦之夜。

1166
00:45:31.650 --> 00:45:32.590
I wasn't there.
我当时不在场。

1167
00:45:32.710 --> 00:45:34.570
I called When Monkeys Attack Me.
我当时的主题叫《当猴子袭击我》。

1168
00:45:35.210 --> 00:45:36.410
I've talked about this.
我聊过这个。

1169
00:45:36.570 --> 00:45:37.510
This is the title?
这是标题？

1170
00:45:37.710 --> 00:45:39.430
When Monkeys Attack Me.
《当猴子袭击我》。

1171
00:45:39.890 --> 00:45:40.690
It's very funny.
非常搞笑。

1172
00:45:40.850 --> 00:45:41.410
That's great.
太棒了。

1173
00:45:41.910 --> 00:45:42.310
Yes.
对。

1174
00:45:42.530 --> 00:45:43.310
Are you still doing it?
你现在还在做吗？

1175
00:45:44.570 --> 00:45:45.530
It was like an improv night.
那有点像即兴表演之夜。

1176
00:45:45.690 --> 00:45:47.250
And when you got a suggestion about...
然后当你得到一个关于……

1177
00:45:47.250 --> 00:45:49.050
It was actually monkeys was a suggestion.
实际上“猴子”就是当时的一个建议。

1178
00:45:49.110 --> 00:45:50.230
And I was like, well...
然后我就想，好吧……

1179
00:45:50.230 --> 00:45:52.410
Well, I knew that one-armed monkey attacked you.
好吧，我知道那只独臂猴子袭击过你。

1180
00:45:52.570 --> 00:45:53.630
Your friend's one-armed monkey.
你朋友的那只独臂猴子。

1181
00:45:53.870 --> 00:45:53.920
Yes.
对。

1182
00:45:53.990 --> 00:45:54.290
Yes.
对。

1183
00:45:54.610 --> 00:45:55.910
Becky's one-armed monkey.
贝基的那只独臂猴子。

1184
00:45:56.090 --> 00:45:56.990
It was a gibbon monkey.
那是一只长臂猿。

1185
00:45:57.390 --> 00:45:57.670
Okay.
好吧。

1186
00:45:57.770 --> 00:45:59.290
This was the 70s in Indonesia.
那是70年代的印度尼西亚。

1187
00:45:59.470 --> 00:46:00.910
And some people had monkeys as pets.
有些人把猴子当宠物养。

1188
00:46:01.010 --> 00:46:02.270
My family did not.
我们家没有。

1189
00:46:02.590 --> 00:46:05.830
But Becky's had rescued this one-armed gibbon.
但贝基家救助了这只独臂长臂猿。

1190
00:46:05.970 --> 00:46:08.230
And they built an enclosure for it.
他们给它建了一个围栏。

1191
00:46:08.350 --> 00:46:11.210
And she brought me inside it to meet the monkey.
然后她带我进去见那只猴子。

1192
00:46:11.210 --> 00:46:15.050
And then it started kind of going through the hair on my arm, like looking for bugs.
接着它开始翻找我胳膊上的汗毛，像是在找虫子一样。

1193
00:46:15.370 --> 00:46:16.810
And Becky laughed.
贝基笑了。

1194
00:46:16.970 --> 00:46:18.910
And I swatted at her like, ha, stop it.
我拍打了一下她，好像在说，哈，别闹了。

1195
00:46:19.070 --> 00:46:22.090
When I swatted at her, this monkey loved Becky.
当我拍打她时，这只猴子可太喜欢贝基了。

1196
00:46:22.350 --> 00:46:24.770
The monkey freaked out, started to bite me.
猴子吓坏了，开始咬我。

1197
00:46:24.950 --> 00:46:29.650
I had a little light jacket on, started to like bite me through my jacket.
我当时穿着一件轻便的外套，它就开始隔着外套咬我。

1198
00:46:29.910 --> 00:46:33.870
And then after that, whenever I was there, it would swing by the kitchen nook.
然后从那以后，只要我在那儿，它就会荡到厨房的角落。

1199
00:46:33.870 --> 00:46:38.830
They had a window, and it would open its legs and piss on the window every time it saw me.
他们那里有个窗户，每次它看到我，就会张开腿朝着窗户撒尿。

1200
00:46:40.150 --> 00:46:41.830
But there's more than that?
但还不止这些？

1201
00:46:41.970 --> 00:46:44.050
You've been attacked by more monkeys than that?
你被比这更多的猴子袭击过吗？

1202
00:46:44.110 --> 00:46:52.870
We went to, when I was in elementary school in Indonesia, you know the word orangutan in Indonesian is orangutan, which means person of the forest, orangutan.
我们去过，我小时候在印度尼西亚上小学的时候，你知道印尼语里猩猩叫orangutan，意思是森林里的人，orangutan。

1203
00:46:53.490 --> 00:46:56.290
So we went to this orangutan sanctuary.
所以我们去了这个猩猩保护区。

1204
00:46:56.930 --> 00:47:00.030
I'm laughing because you assume the listener knows so much.
我在笑是因为你觉得听众知道得这么多。

1205
00:47:00.190 --> 00:47:01.070
No, I didn't know that.
不，我不知道这个。

1206
00:47:01.730 --> 00:47:03.050
Of course I didn't know that.
我当然不知道这个。

1207
00:47:03.050 --> 00:47:05.450
I didn't, exactly, I'm like, why would I do that?
我不知道，真的，我当时想，我为什么要这么做？

1208
00:47:05.730 --> 00:47:14.530
Anyway, we go to this sanctuary, and they have this big mama, orangutan.
总之，我们去了这个保护区，那里有一只猩猩大妈妈。

1209
00:47:15.150 --> 00:47:21.410
And they're letting these like second and third graders, they go up and you get to hold her hand, and you take a picture.
他们让那些差不多二年级和三年级的学生上去，你可以拉着她的手拍张照。

1210
00:47:22.570 --> 00:47:23.250
Uh-oh.
糟糕。

1211
00:47:24.390 --> 00:47:27.610
First of all, we're like the same size because I'm in second grade and I'm tiny.
首先，我们差不多一样大，因为我上二年级，而且我很瘦小。

1212
00:47:27.930 --> 00:47:28.950
Maybe I was first grade.
也许我是一年级。

1213
00:47:29.130 --> 00:47:32.930
Anyway, she holds my hand, and she just starts swinging.
总之，她拉着我的手，然后就开始甩起来。

1214
00:47:33.050 --> 00:47:35.630
Swinging my arm, like swinging my arm.
甩我的胳膊，就像甩我的胳膊一样。

1215
00:47:35.730 --> 00:47:39.610
And then she swung up and then went, boom, and I face planted.
然后她把胳膊甩起来，然后，轰的一声，我来了个脸朝下摔倒。

1216
00:47:40.050 --> 00:47:41.030
Like she swung up.
就像她甩上去一样。

1217
00:47:41.070 --> 00:47:41.650
Like slipped you over?
就像把你掀翻了？

1218
00:47:41.870 --> 00:47:42.990
Like on my face.
就像脸着地一样。

1219
00:47:43.830 --> 00:47:46.090
And, but like she was so happy.
而且，但是她好像非常高兴。

1220
00:47:46.330 --> 00:47:47.710
Like it was like, I don't know.
感觉就像是，我不知道。

1221
00:47:48.250 --> 00:47:50.530
Anyway, so orangutan face planted me.
总之，那只猩猩让我脸朝下摔倒了。

1222
00:47:50.970 --> 00:47:52.210
Is there another one?
还有别的吗？

1223
00:47:52.210 --> 00:47:53.290
There can't be a third one.
不可能还有第三个吧。

1224
00:47:53.390 --> 00:47:53.890
There's a third one.
还有第三个。

1225
00:47:54.210 --> 00:47:55.130
Rule of threes.
事不过三。

1226
00:47:55.130 --> 00:47:58.030
So, okay, I had the one-armed gibbon bite me.
所以，好吧，我被一只独臂长臂猿咬过。

1227
00:47:58.890 --> 00:48:00.870
Mama orangutan face plant me.
猩猩妈妈让我脸着地摔倒。

1228
00:48:01.090 --> 00:48:02.950
And then I was in Indonesia.
然后我在印度尼西亚。

1229
00:48:03.330 --> 00:48:09.290
Years later, I was older, and I was at Uluwatu, which is this beautiful temple on the ocean.
几年后，我长大了，我在乌鲁瓦图，那是海边的一座美丽寺庙。

1230
00:48:09.590 --> 00:48:11.090
But there are monkeys everywhere.
但到处都是猴子。

1231
00:48:11.290 --> 00:48:16.190
And they say to you, the monkeys are nakal, which means they're kind of like mischievous, right?
他们对你说，这里的猴子是nakal，意思是它们有点顽皮，对吧？

1232
00:48:16.370 --> 00:48:16.550
Sure.
当然。

1233
00:48:18.010 --> 00:48:22.950
And so you have to like, be careful, don't wear glasses, water bottles, no earrings, nothing dangling,
所以你必须小心，不要戴眼镜，不要带水瓶，不要戴耳环，什么都不要垂下来，

1234
00:48:23.050 --> 00:48:24.490
because they'll just jump on you and take them.
因为它们会直接扑到你身上抢走这些东西。

1235
00:48:25.090 --> 00:48:28.030
I had these tiniest hoop earrings.
我戴着那种最小的环形耳环。

1236
00:48:28.190 --> 00:48:29.150
They're so tiny.
它们太小了。

1237
00:48:29.370 --> 00:48:32.050
Like the kind that don't even leave room for your skin.
就像那种连皮肤都容不下的那种。

1238
00:48:32.250 --> 00:48:34.710
You know, they're just flat to your earlobe.
你知道的，它们就贴着你的耳垂。

1239
00:48:34.870 --> 00:48:35.110
Sure.
当然。

1240
00:48:35.110 --> 00:48:36.410
So I thought that doesn't dangle.
所以我想那不会垂下来。

1241
00:48:37.070 --> 00:48:38.130
I'm standing there.
我站在那里。

1242
00:48:38.270 --> 00:48:39.730
I'm looking out at the ocean.
我望着大海。

1243
00:48:39.730 --> 00:48:41.350
I'm like, oh, this is so beautiful.
我心想，哦，这太美了。

1244
00:48:42.210 --> 00:48:44.050
There's a monkey in the tree.
树上有一只猴子。

1245
00:48:44.690 --> 00:48:49.790
It literally torpedo jumps onto my shoulder and rips the earring out of my ear.
它就像一颗鱼雷一样跳到我的肩膀上，把耳环从我耳朵上扯了下来。

1246
00:48:49.930 --> 00:48:50.550
Oh, my God.
噢，天哪。

1247
00:48:50.890 --> 00:48:51.890
It tore your ear?
它把你的耳朵撕裂了？

1248
00:48:52.030 --> 00:48:52.770
No, it didn't.
不，没有。

1249
00:48:52.910 --> 00:48:53.690
It just popped right out.
它一下子就脱落了。

1250
00:48:53.790 --> 00:48:56.370
But I literally turned into the most Southern person.
但我真的变得像个最典型的美国南方人了。

1251
00:48:56.490 --> 00:48:57.830
I was like, oh, my Lord.
我当时就惊呼，我的天呐。

1252
00:48:59.230 --> 00:49:04.190
And then it had my earring up in the tree, and it was kind of like gnawing on my earring.
然后它把我的耳环挂在树上，还有点像是在啃我的耳环。

1253
00:49:04.890 --> 00:49:09.330
And this guy that was kind of guiding everyone through the temple, he had these little bananas.
然后有个带大家参观寺庙的导游，他带着一些小香蕉。

1254
00:49:09.590 --> 00:49:10.450
And he traded.
然后他们就交换了。

1255
00:49:10.610 --> 00:49:12.230
He looked at the monkey, and he was like, you want a banana?
他看着那只猴子，好像在说，你想来根香蕉吗？

1256
00:49:12.670 --> 00:49:14.090
And the monkey's like, you want this earring?
而猴子的意思就像是，你想要这个耳环吗？

1257
00:49:14.210 --> 00:49:15.830
And they went back and forth, and then they traded.
它们你来我往地交涉了一番，然后就成交了。

1258
00:49:16.110 --> 00:49:17.550
And I got my earring back.
然后我的耳环就失而复得啦。

1259
00:49:17.790 --> 00:49:20.310
Oh, so you think the monkey knew to do that to get a banana?
哦，所以你觉得那只猴子懂用这招来换香蕉？

1260
00:49:20.510 --> 00:49:21.270
I don't know.
我不知道。

1261
00:49:21.350 --> 00:49:24.110
I mean, here's my thing about these three incidents.
我的意思是，关于这三起事件，我是这样看的。

1262
00:49:24.630 --> 00:49:27.890
Yes, they all involve primates.
没错，它们都涉及灵长类动物。

1263
00:49:28.070 --> 00:49:28.390
Yes.
对。

1264
00:49:28.710 --> 00:49:31.110
They also all involve Indonesia.
而且它们也都发生在印度尼西亚。

1265
00:49:31.430 --> 00:49:33.270
And trying to domesticate them.
还试图去驯化它们。

1266
00:49:33.590 --> 00:49:34.370
And human error.
以及人类的失误。

1267
00:49:34.830 --> 00:49:36.310
Well, they're all in sanctuary.
好吧，它们都在保护区里。

1268
00:49:37.210 --> 00:49:40.290
All three of these weren't monkeys who should have been near in any scenario.
这三个地方的猴子无论如何都不该出现在那种地方。

1269
00:49:42.230 --> 00:49:42.630
Okay.
好吧。

1270
00:49:42.790 --> 00:49:48.370
So if you go to a temple anywhere in Bali, the monkeys are there, and you leave them alone.
所以如果你去巴厘岛的任何寺庙，那里到处都是猴子，你别去招惹它们就行。

1271
00:49:48.890 --> 00:49:49.790
It's their temple.
那是它们的寺庙。

1272
00:49:49.990 --> 00:49:51.930
I mean, that's their area, you know?
我是说，那是它们的地盘，你知道吗？

1273
00:49:52.470 --> 00:49:54.290
So you don't mess with them.
所以你别去惹它们。

1274
00:49:54.390 --> 00:49:55.570
But they're everywhere.
但它们无处不在。

1275
00:49:57.330 --> 00:49:59.290
Anyway, I don't know how we got off on that.
总之，我不知道我们怎么扯到这上面来的。

1276
00:49:59.390 --> 00:50:00.590
You asked him if he saw a primate.
你问他有没有见过灵长类动物。

1277
00:50:00.590 --> 00:50:02.950
I just asked if he'd seen the horror film Primate.
我只是问他有没有看过恐怖片《灵长类》。

1278
00:50:03.030 --> 00:50:04.590
So anyway, I'm convinced.
所以无论如何，我确信了。

1279
00:50:04.590 --> 00:50:07.710
Let's say you had a chimpanzee and I went over.
假设你有一只黑猩猩，然后我走过去。

1280
00:50:07.810 --> 00:50:09.550
I'm like, it's coming for me.
我就觉得，它朝我冲过来了。

1281
00:50:09.690 --> 00:50:11.290
I'm never going to have one.
我绝对不会养这玩意儿。

1282
00:50:11.430 --> 00:50:15.510
Well, I am just convinced that monkeys, like, I am not getting around a monkey.
总之我就是坚信，猴子这种动物……反正我是绝不会靠近猴子的。

1283
00:50:15.650 --> 00:50:16.410
It's coming for me.
它肯定是冲我来的。

1284
00:50:16.750 --> 00:50:19.210
I mean, I have not a single monkey story.
我是说，我可连一个关于猴子的故事都没有呢。

1285
00:50:19.350 --> 00:50:19.510
Yeah.
是啊。

1286
00:50:19.630 --> 00:50:25.510
Your ability to drop such deep Angela lore so casually is one of my favorite things about you.
你这种随口就能抛出如此深度的安吉拉冷知识的能力，简直是我最喜欢你的地方之一。

1287
00:50:25.650 --> 00:50:27.390
You've never mentioned this before.
你以前从来没提过这事。

1288
00:50:27.390 --> 00:50:31.650
I swear, I thought you guys knew this in all these years about all the monkeys.
我发誓，我还以为你们这多年来一直都知道这些猴子的事呢。

1289
00:50:32.390 --> 00:50:33.850
I actually have more.
其实我还有更多故事。

1290
00:50:34.050 --> 00:50:35.350
I'll save it for another day.
我留着改天再说吧。

1291
00:50:35.350 --> 00:50:36.790
I can't believe there's more.
真不敢相信居然还有后续。

1292
00:50:37.270 --> 00:50:38.750
I look forward to it.
我拭目以待。

1293
00:50:39.090 --> 00:50:40.390
Well, this was a tangent.
好吧，这话题扯远了。

1294
00:50:41.410 --> 00:50:43.290
It's a true classic tangent.
这绝对是一次经典的跑题。

1295
00:50:43.710 --> 00:50:45.070
Well, I've got a fact.
好吧，我有个冷知识。

1296
00:50:45.450 --> 00:50:48.450
Do you want me to bring us back to the episode with a little fact?
你想让我用一个小知识把大家带回正题，聊聊这集的内容吗？

1297
00:50:48.450 --> 00:50:50.470
I'm sure everybody wants you to bring us back.
我敢说大家都巴不得你把我们带回正题呢。

1298
00:50:50.650 --> 00:50:53.150
Everyone listening right now is like, good Lord.
现在正在收听节目的每个人心里都在想：我的天呐。

1299
00:50:53.510 --> 00:50:54.110
All right.
好吧。

1300
00:50:54.210 --> 00:50:57.270
Well, listen, when Ned shows up at this bar,
听着，当内德出现在这家酒吧时，

1301
00:50:57.910 --> 00:51:01.110
his face is like peeling off in huge sections.
他的脸就像是有大片大片的东西在剥落。

1302
00:51:01.110 --> 00:51:02.130
It's like red.
呈现出一种红色。

1303
00:51:02.290 --> 00:51:03.850
It's flaking off.
它正在脱皮。

1304
00:51:03.950 --> 00:51:07.910
And I was really curious, how did they do this?
我当时真的很好奇，他们是怎么做到的？

1305
00:51:07.990 --> 00:51:12.270
Because we know that this would have been like an elaborate makeup teSt.
因为我们知道这本该是一次精心设计的妆容测试。

1306
00:51:13.170 --> 00:51:15.290
And it also would have had to have continuity.
而且它还必须具备连贯性。

1307
00:51:15.530 --> 00:51:15.790
Yes.
是的。

1308
00:51:15.790 --> 00:51:19.210
Like, okay, this is the fifth hour into this face mask.
比如，好吧，这是戴着这个面具的第五个小时。

1309
00:51:19.330 --> 00:51:20.110
What does that look like?
那会是什么样子？

1310
00:51:20.210 --> 00:51:20.730
And it does.
确实如此。

1311
00:51:20.890 --> 00:51:22.070
His face progresses.
他的脸在不断变化。

1312
00:51:22.130 --> 00:51:23.530
It gets worse and worse.
情况越来越糟。

1313
00:51:23.530 --> 00:51:28.190
So I reached out to Kelly Cantley, who put me in touch with Autumn Butler, the makeup
所以我联系了凯利·坎特利，她帮我联系了秋·巴特勒，本集的

1314
00:51:28.190 --> 00:51:29.410
artist for this episode.
化妆师。

1315
00:51:29.610 --> 00:51:31.090
Thank you so much, Kelly.
非常感谢你，凯利。

1316
00:51:31.750 --> 00:51:38.810
And Autumn said this was a very fun makeup to design and that Greg Daniels had very specific
秋说，设计这个妆容非常有趣，而且格雷格·丹尼尔斯有非常具体的

1317
00:51:38.810 --> 00:51:39.490
ideas.
想法。

1318
00:51:40.010 --> 00:51:46.810
Greg definitely did not want it to look or feel like an actual condition that somebody
格雷格绝对不想让它看起来或让人感觉像是什么人在现实生活中

1319
00:51:46.810 --> 00:51:48.210
would really have in real life.
真正会患上的某种实际病症。

1320
00:51:48.330 --> 00:51:53.970
He didn't want anyone to feel like they were being made fun of about any actual real life
他不想让任何人觉得他们正在被嘲笑他们可能正在经历的任何

1321
00:51:53.970 --> 00:51:55.490
problem they might be experiencing.
现实生活中的实际问题。

1322
00:51:56.470 --> 00:52:02.990
He also wanted it to feel very, as Autumn put it, charismatically comedic.
正如秋所说，他还希望它给人一种非常具有个人魅力的喜剧感。

1323
00:52:02.990 --> 00:52:03.590
Hmm.
嗯。

1324
00:52:04.150 --> 00:52:09.750
So Autumn said they tested this makeup for two days to find the perfect look and texture.
所以秋说他们对这个妆容进行了两天的测试，以找到完美的造型和质感。

1325
00:52:10.290 --> 00:52:16.450
Greg really wanted it to look like a snake that was like molting and shedding in sheets
格雷格真的很希望它看起来像一条蛇在成片成层地

1326
00:52:16.450 --> 00:52:17.090
and layers.
蜕皮。

1327
00:52:17.390 --> 00:52:19.330
Oh, it does look like that by the end.
哦，到最后看起来确实是那样。

1328
00:52:19.510 --> 00:52:23.410
He also wanted pieces that could be peeled away on camera.
他还想要那些能在镜头前被撕下来的碎片。

1329
00:52:23.510 --> 00:52:30.450
So they had to create both this makeup that was on his face and also this interactive piece.
所以他们既要打造他脸上这个妆容，还要制作这个互动道具。

1330
00:52:30.450 --> 00:52:33.650
So Autumn said first they tried it with silicone.
秋说他们最初是用硅胶尝试的。

1331
00:52:33.870 --> 00:52:36.730
They tried melted pieces of bald caps.
他们尝试了融化的秃头套碎片。

1332
00:52:36.970 --> 00:52:40.310
They tried latex strips, but nothing was giving the right feel.
他们尝试了乳胶条，但没有一种能达到那种感觉。

1333
00:52:40.690 --> 00:52:50.330
So in the end, she created a mixture of Elmer's glue and duo eyelash glue applied to his face
所以最后，她用白乳胶和杜奥假睫毛胶混合涂在他的脸上，

1334
00:52:50.330 --> 00:52:51.790
in really thin layers.
涂得很薄很薄。

1335
00:52:51.910 --> 00:52:57.390
And then they scrunched up his face and started peeling portions off.
然后他们挤皱他的脸，开始撕下一部分。

1336
00:52:57.390 --> 00:53:01.210
She said it was like a total old-fashioned arts and crafts project.
她说这就像是一个彻头彻尾的老式工艺美术项目。

1337
00:53:02.010 --> 00:53:04.710
I mean, how was his skin in real life?
我是说，他在现实生活中的皮肤怎么样？

1338
00:53:04.890 --> 00:53:06.030
I didn't ask her.
我没问她。

1339
00:53:07.690 --> 00:53:09.470
I mean, he's wearing glue.
我是说，他涂了胶水嘛。

1340
00:53:09.810 --> 00:53:17.010
But she said they also made sheets of fake skin with that same Elmer's lash glue mixture,
但她说他们还用那种白乳胶和睫毛胶的混合物制作了假皮肤片，

1341
00:53:17.010 --> 00:53:23.150
and they spread it out on wax paper, and then they let it dry, and then they would peel that off.
他们把它铺在蜡纸上，然后让它风干，接着再把它撕下来。

1342
00:53:23.150 --> 00:53:26.270
And those were the pieces that they would use.
那些就是他们会用到的碎片。

1343
00:53:26.630 --> 00:53:29.470
Like, they would just attach it very slightly to his skin,
比如，他们只会把它非常轻微地贴在他的皮肤上，

1344
00:53:29.470 --> 00:53:32.590
and then that would be the piece that he, like, pulled off interactively.
然后那就会成为他互动撕下来的那块东西。

1345
00:53:33.610 --> 00:53:38.250
And then Eric said he remembered the test process for this whole thing.
然后埃里克说他记得这一切的测试过程。

1346
00:53:38.410 --> 00:53:39.910
He said it was very thorough.
他说非常彻底。

1347
00:53:40.170 --> 00:53:45.050
He remembered Autumn from makeup, hired somebody to do the test makeup.
他记得化妆师秋雇了个人来做测试妆。

1348
00:53:45.970 --> 00:53:47.530
Isn't that a crazy job?
这不是一份疯狂的工作吗？

1349
00:53:47.730 --> 00:53:47.930
Yeah.
是啊。

1350
00:53:47.930 --> 00:53:51.710
You get hired to just come in and let them test stuff on you.
你被雇来只是为了过来让他们在你身上测试各种东西。

1351
00:53:52.110 --> 00:53:53.350
I mean, yeah.
我的意思是，对吧。

1352
00:53:53.610 --> 00:53:53.890
Yeah.
对。

1353
00:53:54.110 --> 00:53:59.350
So anyway, Eric said that Autumn brought this guy into the writer's room.
所以不管怎样，埃里克说奥秋姆把这小子带进了编剧室。

1354
00:53:59.730 --> 00:54:04.410
He thinks it was, like, four times before Greg approved the makeup.
他觉得大概有四次之多，格雷格才通过了那个妆容。

1355
00:54:04.870 --> 00:54:06.970
Look how much went into this one gag.
瞧瞧这一个包袱花的心思有多大。

1356
00:54:07.190 --> 00:54:07.810
I know!
我懂！

1357
00:54:08.110 --> 00:54:08.450
Wow.
哇。

1358
00:54:08.990 --> 00:54:10.110
Eric also said,
埃里克还说，

1359
00:54:10.270 --> 00:54:13.410
if I were Ned, I would have gone to the hospital if my skin looked like that.
要我是内德，我的皮肤要是长成那样，我早就去医院了。

1360
00:54:13.530 --> 00:54:16.370
But I understand he's just very passionate about journalism.
不过我理解，他对新闻事业就是充满热情。

1361
00:54:16.370 --> 00:54:16.850
Yeah.
对。

1362
00:54:17.130 --> 00:54:21.630
Well, we do find out that, in the end, his skin ends up looking amazing.
不过，我们最后发现，他的皮肤到头来好得不得了。

1363
00:54:21.630 --> 00:54:23.450
The next day, he's, like, glowing.
第二天，他整个人简直是在发光。

1364
00:54:23.790 --> 00:54:24.130
Glowing.
发光。

1365
00:54:24.130 --> 00:54:25.210
It comes around.
苦尽甘来嘛。

1366
00:54:25.550 --> 00:54:29.990
And just to keep throwing facts at you, I have a location breakdown for the Macaroni Barn.
为了继续给你抛出干货，我手头有一份通心粉小屋的取景分析。

1367
00:54:30.790 --> 00:54:36.070
First of all, there's no Macaroni Barn in Toledo, Ohio, but there is a spaghetti warehouse.
首先，俄亥俄州托莱多根本没有什么通心粉小屋，但有一家意大利面仓库。

1368
00:54:37.210 --> 00:54:37.770
Coincidence?
巧合吗？

1369
00:54:39.490 --> 00:54:40.330
Inspired by?
灵感来源？

1370
00:54:40.850 --> 00:54:41.410
Perhaps.
也许吧。

1371
00:54:41.410 --> 00:54:41.610
Perhaps.
也许吧。

1372
00:54:42.610 --> 00:54:47.350
Eric shared that the interior and exterior of the Macaroni Barn were two different places.
埃里克透露，通心粉小屋的内景和外景是两个不同的地方。

1373
00:54:48.090 --> 00:54:49.110
We've done that before.
我们以前也这么干过。

1374
00:54:49.230 --> 00:54:50.850
We did that with Poor Richard's on The Office.
我们在《办公室》里拍“可怜的理查德”时就这样做过。

1375
00:54:51.150 --> 00:54:51.290
Yep.
没错。

1376
00:54:51.810 --> 00:54:56.750
The interior of Macaroni Barn was shot at the Smokehouse next to the Universal lot.
通心粉小屋的内景是在环球影城地块旁边的烟屋拍摄的。

1377
00:54:56.750 --> 00:55:07.330
And the exterior is actually a fakie front restaurant on the Universal lot right across from the high school, from Back to the Future.
而外景实际上是环球影城里的一家假门面餐厅，就在《回到未来》里那个高中的正对面。

1378
00:55:07.830 --> 00:55:13.390
So, if you go on the little Universal bus tour, you could see it.
所以，如果你去坐环球影城的电瓶观光车，就能看到它。

1379
00:55:14.310 --> 00:55:18.750
So, the following morning, we do have this little wrap-up scene between Ken and Adam.
所以，第二天早上，肯和亚当之间确实有这么一小场收尾戏。

1380
00:55:19.510 --> 00:55:21.130
I just loved Ken in this episode.
我太喜欢这集里的肯了。

1381
00:55:21.270 --> 00:55:22.770
I get why Eric loved writing for him.
我懂为什么埃里克那么喜欢为他写台词了。

1382
00:55:22.910 --> 00:55:24.570
Ken says, how are you feeling?
肯说，你感觉怎么样？

1383
00:55:24.690 --> 00:55:28.250
More importantly, did you make mad, ravenous scorpion love to your wife?
更重要的是，你跟你的妻子进行狂野、如狼似虎的蝎子式爱爱了吗？

1384
00:55:28.710 --> 00:55:30.930
We find out from Adam they did it, like, three times.
我们从亚当那里得知他们做了大概三次。

1385
00:55:31.010 --> 00:55:32.690
And Ken's like, wowee, three times.
然后肯就说，哇塞，三次。

1386
00:55:32.850 --> 00:55:33.850
Big man, love that.
真行，爱了爱了。

1387
00:55:34.470 --> 00:55:38.570
And then Adam's like, maybe they were just sugar pills, because three times is pretty standard for us.
接着亚当就说，也许那些只是糖丸吧，因为三次对我们来说挺正常的。

1388
00:55:39.250 --> 00:55:41.190
I mean, no wonder he has four kids.
我的天，难怪他有四个孩子。

1389
00:55:41.190 --> 00:55:41.530
I wonder.
我也觉得。

1390
00:55:42.150 --> 00:55:43.350
Snip, snap, Adam.
咔哒，咔哒，亚当。

1391
00:55:43.810 --> 00:55:48.970
And then we have a little hint at maybe a romance.
然后我们迎来了一个暗示可能萌芽的恋情的小彩蛋。

1392
00:55:50.050 --> 00:55:50.810
Between who?
在谁和谁之间？

1393
00:55:51.410 --> 00:55:52.230
Ned and Mare.
内德和梅尔。

1394
00:55:52.770 --> 00:55:58.950
He clearly thought she looked beautiful, but he was like, listen, I'm sorry if Esmeralda made you dress up like that.
他显然觉得她看起来很美，但他却说，听着，如果埃斯梅拉达让你打扮成那样，我很抱歉。

1395
00:55:59.150 --> 00:56:00.990
I know that's not something you like.
我知道这不是你喜欢的事。

1396
00:56:01.190 --> 00:56:02.350
She's like, what are you talking about?
她就说，你在说什么呢？

1397
00:56:02.430 --> 00:56:03.230
I like dressing up.
我喜欢打扮。

1398
00:56:03.610 --> 00:56:06.950
And he was like, yeah, but, you know, you're asexual, so.
而他说，对啊，但是，你知道的，你是无性恋，所以。

1399
00:56:07.130 --> 00:56:08.670
And she was like, why would you think that?
然后她就说，你为什么会这么想？

1400
00:56:09.010 --> 00:56:10.770
And then he's like, Esmeralda!
紧接着他就喊，埃斯梅拉达！

1401
00:56:11.450 --> 00:56:13.210
And he's so ticked off.
而且他气坏了。

1402
00:56:13.330 --> 00:56:14.750
He's like, Esmeralda, you told me.
他就像是在说，埃斯梅拉达，你告诉过我的。

1403
00:56:14.970 --> 00:56:16.950
And Mare's like, it doesn't matter what she told you.
而梅尔则说，她告诉你什么根本不重要。

1404
00:56:17.250 --> 00:56:18.550
What kind of journalist are you?
你算什么记者？

1405
00:56:18.670 --> 00:56:19.590
You didn't even ask me?
你甚至都没问我？

1406
00:56:19.790 --> 00:56:20.790
You didn't even follow up?
你甚至都没有跟进？

1407
00:56:21.290 --> 00:56:22.910
But I mean, he's her boss.
但我的意思是，他是她的老板。

1408
00:56:23.030 --> 00:56:25.470
How can he go to her and ask her about her sexuality?
他怎么能去找她并盘问她的性取向呢？

1409
00:56:25.490 --> 00:56:26.670
He's not allowed to do that.
他不被允许这么做。

1410
00:56:26.730 --> 00:56:27.070
I know.
我知道。

1411
00:56:27.230 --> 00:56:28.850
So it's like, I get it.
所以感觉就是，我懂。

1412
00:56:28.850 --> 00:56:35.570
Like, I thought it was cool of him to be like, hey, listen, I hope that whole thing didn't put you in an uncomfortable situation.
就像，我觉得他挺酷的，会说，嘿，听着，我希望整件事没有把你置于尴尬的境地。

1413
00:56:36.450 --> 00:56:44.450
In general, you shouldn't have to be, you know, flirting with men and sources in order to get, you know, a story.
总的来说，为了搞到一条新闻，你本不该去和男人还有消息源调情的，你知道的。

1414
00:56:44.730 --> 00:56:45.370
And I just, you know.
而我只是，你知道的。

1415
00:56:45.370 --> 00:56:46.650
He was trying to be appropriate.
他是在试图表现得得体。

1416
00:56:46.650 --> 00:56:47.190
He was.
他是的。

1417
00:56:47.730 --> 00:56:49.890
Well, this episode ends with the Ned talking head.
好吧，这一集在内德的单人访谈中结束了。

1418
00:56:50.010 --> 00:56:51.090
He's just perplexed.
他整个人百思不得其解。

1419
00:56:51.110 --> 00:56:52.430
He's like, why is she mad at me?
他就像在说，她为什么生我的气？

1420
00:56:52.670 --> 00:56:54.050
Some people are just sensitive.
有些人就是比较敏感。

1421
00:56:54.050 --> 00:56:57.650
And then he's like, she didn't even notice how revitalized I look.
然后他说，她甚至都没注意到我看起来多么焕然一新。

1422
00:56:59.170 --> 00:56:59.690
Exactly.
完全正确。

1423
00:57:00.350 --> 00:57:02.450
And that's the end of the episode, everybody.
这就是这一集的结尾啦，各位。

1424
00:57:02.750 --> 00:57:07.250
Thank you to everyone who sent in their around the towns and to Darby for our chit chat.
感谢所有发来各地趣闻的朋友，也感谢达比和我们聊天。

1425
00:57:07.550 --> 00:57:07.930
Yes.
是的。

1426
00:57:08.030 --> 00:57:18.650
And also a big thank you to Eric Rahill, Kelly Cantley, Autumn Butler, Sabrina Impaciatore, and Chelsea Fry for some great behind-the-scenes nuggets on this one.
还要非常感谢埃里克·拉希尔、凯利·坎特利、奥特姆·巴特勒、萨布里娜·因帕恰托雷和切尔西·弗莱，感谢他们为这一集提供的精彩幕后花絮。

1427
00:57:18.870 --> 00:57:19.150
Great.
太棒了。

1428
00:57:19.270 --> 00:57:20.650
Before we go, I have something for you guys.
在我们离开之前，我给你们大家准备了个东西。

1429
00:57:20.890 --> 00:57:22.130
